    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f48456b06a7982eb9e7b73966a12a668d9872697fd9b7efd2f0cd2c971ab6bd1",
      "text": "Transfer to El Chaltén. On arrival, you’ll set out on the hike to Laguna Capri.\n\nThis half-day route is for anyone who wants to see Fitz Roy without a long hike. The trail starts at the far end of the village, by an old house known as the Yellow Chair.\n\nThe first section climbs steadily for about an hour, with stops to rest and take photos. Along the way, you’ll see the Río de las Vueltas valley and catch your first views of Fitz Roy. This short hike works well after the drive from El Calafate and gives you a view of the area’s main mountain range within half a day.\n\nAfter around 45 minutes, you’ll reach the first viewpoint, with views of the Fitz Roy massif and the surrounding peaks of Poincenot, Saint-Exupéry, Mermoz and Guillaumet.\n\nThe trail forks near the viewpoint. One branch leads to Laguna Capri, a forest-fringed lake with a campsite nearby. The return to El Chaltén is mostly downhill.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6kyprr-kcrymv07az",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      }
